    "intro_narrative": "You awaken in the abandoned Chronos Research Facility. The air is stale, and emergency lights flicker, casting long shadows across the cold metallic walls. Once a hub for cutting-edge temporal experiments, this laboratory now stands silent, completely sealed off from the outside world. Your mission is of absolute importance: you must recover the highly classified timezone text, a critical piece of data that could stabilize the current temporal anomaly threatening your reality. The text is secured somewhere within this room, protected by layers of advanced security and scrambled equipment. As you look around, you notice various dormant devices, terminals, and strange data drives scattered across the desks and floor. The automated systems are barely functional, requiring precise manual operations and logical deduction to restore the correct data flow. You will need to carefully investigate every piece of surviving equipment, figure out how they connect, and bypass the rigorous biometric defenses. With the facility's life support systems slowly failing and the ambient temperature dropping, time is of the essence. Stay sharp, trust your instincts, and navigate the fragmented technology to secure the archive before this laboratory becomes your permanent tomb.",
    "narrative_style": "sci_fi"
